# otto-factory — machine-level config
#
# This file stays in the otto-factory folder and holds settings that are the
# same for every project on this machine: the paths to your CLI tools and
# global timeout/retry defaults.
#
# Project-specific settings (GITHUB_REPO, TEST_COMMAND, SOURCE_GLOB) go in a
# .otto file inside each project folder — see .otto.example for that template.
#
# Copy this file to .env and uncomment the lines you need to change.

# ── Tool paths (only change if `which gh` / `which claude` returns a custom path) ───
# GH_BIN=gh
# CLAUDE_BIN=claude

# ── Global defaults (can be overridden per-project in .otto) ─────────────────

# Timeout in seconds for the coder agent (default: 600)
# CODER_TIMEOUT=600

# Maximum retry attempts per issue (default: 3)
# MAX_ATTEMPTS=3

# Shell initialisation command prepended to TEST_COMMAND before running tests.
#
# otto-factory runs TEST_COMMAND in a non-interactive bash shell, which does NOT
# source your ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc. If your test runner (node, python, ruby, etc.)
# is managed by a version manager, you need to initialise it here so it is on PATH.
#
# How to find the right value:
#   1. Run `which npm` (or `which python`, `which node`, etc.) in your terminal.
#   2. If the path contains ".nvm", ".asdf", ".pyenv", or similar, you need SHELL_INIT.
#   3. Check your ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc for the line that loads your version manager
#      and paste it here.
#
# Common examples:
#   SHELL_INIT=source ~/.nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use node --silent   # nvm (Node.js)
#   SHELL_INIT=source ~/.asdf/asdf.sh                          # asdf (multi-language)
#   SHELL_INIT=source ~/.rvm/scripts/rvm                       # rvm (Ruby)
#
# If `which npm` returns a standard path like /usr/local/bin/npm you don't need this.
#
# SHELL_INIT=
